      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* --- The algebra: boosts do not close --- */\neps(i,j,k) := (j-i)*(k-i)*(k-j)/2$\nLg : [L1,L2,L3]$  Kg : [K1,K2,K3]$\n\nprint(\"commutators in so(1,3):\")$\nprint(\"   [Lᵢ,Lⱼ] − ε_ijk Lₖ :\")$\nfor i:1 thru 3 do for j:i+1 thru 3 do block([k], k : 6-i-j,\n  print(\"      i=\", i, \" j=\", j, \" : \",\n        br(Lg[i],Lg[j]) - eps(i,j,k)*Lg[k]))$\nprint(\"   [Lᵢ,Kⱼ] − ε_ijk Kₖ :\")$\nfor i:1 thru 3 do for j:i+1 thru 3 do block([k], k : 6-i-j,\n  print(\"      i=\", i, \" j=\", j, \" : \",\n        br(Lg[i],Kg[j]) - eps(i,j,k)*Kg[k]))$\nprint(\"   [Kᵢ,Kⱼ] + ε_ijk Lₖ :\")$\nfor i:1 thru 3 do for j:i+1 thru 3 do block([k], k : 6-i-j,\n  print(\"      i=\", i, \" j=\", j, \" : \",\n        br(Kg[i],Kg[j]) + eps(i,j,k)*Lg[k]))$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"Read the three blocks:\")$\nprint(\"   rotations close on themselves — so(3) ⊂ so(1,3) is a subalgebra\")$\nprint(\"   [rotation, boost] = boost — boosts form a vector under rotation\")$\nprint(\"   [boost, boost] = −rotation — BOOSTS DO NOT CLOSE.\")$\nprint(\"The minus sign in the last line is the signature showing through;\")$\nprint(\"in so(4) it would be a plus, and in so(3) the K's would BE L's.\")$\n\n/* --- Thomas precession, at the group level --- */\n/* By BCH (5.02), Λx(φ)Λy(ψ)Λx(−φ)Λy(−ψ) ≈ exp(φψ[K₁,K₂]) = exp(−φψ L₃)\n   to leading order.  Expand both sides in a common small parameter. */\nbx(r) := matrixmap(hs, matrixexp(r*K1))$\nby(r) := matrixmap(hs, matrixexp(r*K2))$\nCcom : hsm( bx(aa*ss) . by(bb*ss) . bx(-aa*ss) . by(-bb*ss) )$\nCexp : matrixmap(lambda([e], ratdisrep(taylor(e, ss, 0, 2))), Ccom)$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"THOMAS PRECESSION.  The group commutator of two boosts,\")$\nprint(\"Λx(as)Λy(bs)Λx(−as)Λy(−bs), expanded to O(s²):\")$\nprint(\"   \", Cexp)$\nprint(\"   predicted I + s²ab[K₁,K₂] = I − s²ab L₃ = \",\n      ident(4) - ss^2*aa*bb*L3)$\nprint(\"   difference = \",\n      ratsimp( Cexp - (ident(4) - ss^2*aa*bb*L3) ))$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"A closed loop of pure boosts returns a ROTATION.  A gyroscope\")$\nprint(\"carried round it comes back turned — Thomas precession, measurable\")$\nprint(\"in atomic spectra.  It is holonomy again (4.02): transport around a\")$\nprint(\"loop, return with a rotation, and the infinitesimal generator of\")$\nprint(\"that rotation is a bracket.\")$",
      "metadata": {},
