          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "the Hermitian-matrix picture of a 4-vector:\n   X(v) =  matrix([zv+tv,xv-%i*yv],[%i*yv+xv,tv-zv])\n   det X =  -zv^2-yv^2-xv^2+tv^2\n   det X + ⟨v,v⟩ =  0\n   so the Minkowski norm IS a determinant.  Anything preserving\n   det therefore acts by Lorentz transformations.\n   for ANY A ∈ GL(2,ℂ):\n      det(A X A†) − |det A|² det X =  0\n   so det A = 1 ⟹ |det A|² = 1 ⟹ det is preserved ⟹ X ↦ A X A†\n   is a Lorentz transformation.  SL(2,ℂ) acts on Minkowski space.\n   A = diag(e^{φ/2}, e^{−φ/2}) :\n      t′ =  (%e^-phv*((%e^(2*phv)-1)*zv+(%e^(2*phv)+1)*tv))/2\n      z′ =  (%e^-phv*((%e^(2*phv)+1)*zv+(%e^(2*phv)-1)*tv))/2\n      x′ =  xv      y′ =  yv\nProviso: assuming 4*phv # 0\n      compared with exp(φK₃) applied to v, difference =  [0,0,0,0]\n      A boost in z, exactly.  SU(2) ⊂ SL(2,ℂ) gives the rotations\n      in the same way — the case 1.03 and 5.01 already did.\n   ±A give the SAME Lorentz transformation:\n      (−A)X(−A)† − A X A† =  matrix([0,0],[0,0])\n   So SL(2,ℂ) → SO⁺(1,3) is 2-to-1: a double cover, exactly as\n   SU(2) → SO(3) was in 1.03.  One signature over, same phenomenon —\n   and the reason spinors exist in relativity at all.\n   dimension check:  sl(2,ℂ) as a REAL Lie algebra has dimension\n  6  = 2(n²−1) with n = 2,\n   and dim so(1,3) =  6 .  Equal ✓, as an isomorphism needs.\n   The duality m ↦ i·m that 5.04 used to turn so(3) into so(2,1) is\n   the same complexification seen from the other side."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* The light cone and the orbits of the boost group.\n   Horizontal axis x, vertical axis y = time.  (The plot variables must be\n   called x and y; nothing above assigns to them, deliberately.) */\nplot2d([ y = x, y = -x, y^2 - x^2 = 1, x^2 - y^2 = 1 ],\n  [x, -3, 3], [y, -3, 3],\n  [legend, \"light cone t = x\", \"light cone t = -x\",\n           \"t² − x² = 1  (timelike, one clock-tick)\",\n           \"x² − t² = 1  (spacelike, one ruler-length)\"],\n  [xlabel, \"x\"], [ylabel, \"t\"],\n  [title, \"Minkowski space: the light cone and the orbits of a boost\"],\n  [style, [lines,2], [lines,2], [lines,3], [lines,3]])$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 12,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
